For $z = i,$ the area of the square is
\[|z^2 - z|^2 = |z|^2 |z - 1|^2 = |i|^2 |i - 1|^2 = 2.\]For $z = -i$, the area of the square is
\[|z^2 - z|^2 = |z|^2 |z - 1|^2 = |-i|^2 |-i - 1|^2 = 2.\]The final case is where $z^3$ is between $z$ and $z^2.$


