solution:
To find $f^{-1}(-31/96)$, we need to find the value of $x$ that satisfies $f(x)=-31/96$.
We start by setting $f(x)=-31/96$ and solving for $x$:
\begin{align*}
\frac{x^5-1}3&=-\frac{31}{96}\\
x^5-1&=-\frac{31}{32}\\
x^5&=1-\frac{31}{32}=\frac{1}{32}\\
x&=\sqrt[5]{\frac{1}{32}}=\frac{1}{2}.
\end{align*}
Therefore, $f^{-1}(-31/96)=\boxed{\frac{1}{2}}$.
The answer is \frac{1}{2}

